{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>Molten elohim.</b> These are the talismans made at determined times under a particular configuration of the stars. Therefore they are made by means of casting, in order that all the parts of their forms come into being together in the same instant. Their makers intend through them to obtain acquisitions and bodily needs, and the maker may suppose that this is not rebellion against El blessed be He, so long as the one who worships them does not accept them as a deity. Yet it is in truth contrary to His will, for He desires that His servants not turn for help to any elohim besides Him, as it says: וְאַנְחְנוּ לֹא נֵדַע מַה נַּעֲשֶׂה כִּי עָלֶיךָ עֵינֵינוּ (II Chronicles 20:12)."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {0 "The quotation reads וְאַנְחְנוּ but the biblical text has וַאֲנַחְנוּ; retained Sforno's spelling as given."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:28:07.573867191Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}